FINAL ANSWER:
Review by **Troy Goode** first. **Douglas Christopher Wilson** and **Alejandro Caravaca Puchades** are second and third, but neither has committed in years.

`surviving-lines --reviewers lib/index.js` counted 214 non-blank lines (238 with blank lines) at HEAD, using `git blame -w -M -C` (default copy detection):

| # | Reviewer | Surviving lines | Share | Commits | Last commit | Activity |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Troy Goode (2 addresses) | 144 | 67.3% | 29 | 2026-04-10 | active |
| 2 | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 20 | 9.3% | 4 | 2017-10-04 | inactive |
| 3 | Alejandro Caravaca Puchades | 14 | 6.5% | 5 | 2015-05-28 | inactive |
| 4 | LuisEGR | 6 | 2.8% | 1 | 2021-07-20 | inactive |
| 5 | Raymond Feng | 6 | 2.8% | 1 | 2015-01-13 | inactive |

19 more authors hold the rest of the lines. The order is by surviving lines. "Active" only means a commit in the 365 days before 2026-04-12, and it does not change the order. Troy is the only active owner, so for a fast review ask Troy. If the change touches what Douglas or Alejandro wrote, they are still worth asking.

**Things to know about these numbers:**
- **Troy Goode is probably counted twice.** Troy appears under `<email redacted>` (132 lines, 61.7%) and `troy@laptop.example` (12 lines, 5.6%). The same name makes this a strong match, so I combined them into the 144 figure. This is still a guess from names and addresses. Only you can confirm it is one person. I did not write a `.mailmap`.
- **Alejandro is already counted once.** Commits under "Alejandro Caravaca Puchades" and "alex94puchades" use the same address, so the tool counts them as one person.
- **A reformat commit was set aside.** Commit `62628c0` by Fiona Formatter ("style: reformat js…") only changed whitespace and quotes in 4 files (1,016 lines added, 1,016 removed). If it were counted, it would take 32 lines in this file. Troy would drop from 144 to 123 (57.5%), Douglas from 20 to 16 (7.5%) and Alejandro from 14 to 13 (6.1%). Fiona reformatted the file but did not write it, so Fiona is not a reviewer to ask.
- **Mechanical rewrites were checked.** The tool looked at 31 commits and set aside `62628c0`. It flagged `fcd2b56` (Troy's ESLint cleanup, 2015) but kept it. When I re-ran without that commit, the top 3 did not change.
- **Bus factor is 1.** This means one author alone holds at least 50% of this file's surviving lines: Troy holds 67.3% (66.8% counting blank lines). Three authors together hold 80%. Without combining Troy's two addresses, it is still 1, and it takes 4 authors to reach 80%.

The tool only counts whose lines are still in the file. It does not show code quality, review work or design work, and it cannot tell who understands the code best.
